# MASTER IMPLEMENTATION PROMPT: DEPANEH AUTOMOTIVE SPARE-PARTS MARKETPLACE

## 1. PROJECT OVERVIEW AND OBJECTIVE

I have an existing automotive spare-parts marketplace currently branded as GM Spare/GMSPARE. I have attached a Figma PDF containing the new UI/UX design I want to implement.

Your task is to redesign the existing application to match the attached Figma design and completely rebrand it as DEPANEH.

This is an existing application, not a new project. The existing source code contains important business logic, routes, integrations, data models, authentication, permissions, and workflows that must be preserved.

The finished application must combine:

- The visual design and user experience of the attached Figma PDF.
- The functionality and business logic of the existing application.
- A consistent, application-wide DEPANEH brand identity.
- A complete interface for buyers/mechanics, dealers, delivery riders, and administrators.
- Functional, responsive, maintainable, and production-oriented implementation.

**Primary rule: change the presentation without breaking the functionality.**

Do not create a static prototype, rebuild the application from scratch unnecessarily, or replace working backend functionality with mock data.

